Current Scope

Laboratory-scale pintle valve
Water-based flow loop
Closed-loop control
Flow and pressure sensing
Simulation dashboard
Data logging
Cavitation-risk monitoring concept


Future Scope

Improved valve geometry
Higher-accuracy sensors
Advanced control algorithms
Experimental cavitation detection using vibration/acoustic signals
Hardware-to-cloud telemetry
Digital-twin development
CFD-based validation
More advanced risk prediction models
Hardware-in-the-loop testing


Limitations

This project is a research prototype and has several limitations:

It does not replicate cryogenic fluid behaviour.
It does not reproduce rocket combustion.
It does not represent a flight-qualified propulsion component.
The prototype throttle range is limited by laboratory hardware.
Cavitation-risk estimation initially depends on measured flow and pressure parameters.
Experimental results must be obtained through physical testing and are not assumed in advance.
